{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Initializing the SDK","level":2,"anchor":"Initializing-the-SDK"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An instance of the Appcues iOS SDK ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues"},{"type":"text","text":") should be initialized when your app launches. A lifecycle method such as "},{"code":"application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would be a common location:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func application(_ application: UIApplication, didFinishLaunchingWithOptions launchOptions: [UIApplication.LaunchOptionsKey: Any]?) -> Bool {","  let appcuesConfig = Appcues.Config(","    accountID: <#APPCUES_ACCOUNT_ID#>,","    applicationID: <#APPCUES_APPLICATION_ID#>)","    ","  appcues = Appcues(config: appcuesConfig)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/Config"},{"type":"text","text":" object has a number of properties that may optionally be set to customize the behavior of the SDK."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializing the SDK requires you to provide two values, an Appcues account ID, and an Appcues mobile application ID. These values can be obtained from your "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/studio.appcues.com\/settings\/account"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Managing Users","level":2,"anchor":"Managing-Users"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In order to target content to the right users at the right time, you need to identify users and send Appcues data about them. A user is identified with a unique ID."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/identify(userID:properties:)","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more detail about session management and anonymous user tracking, refer to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Identifying"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Tracking Screens and Events","level":2,"anchor":"Tracking-Screens-and-Events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Events are the “actions” your users take in your application, which can be anything from clicking a certain button to viewing a specific screen. Once you’ve installed and initialized the Appcues iOS SDK, you can start tracking screens and events using the following methods:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/track(name:properties:)","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/screen(title:properties:)","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more detail about tracking screens and events, refer to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Tracking"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Anchored Tooltips","level":2,"anchor":"Anchored-Tooltips"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchored tooltips use element targeting to point directly at specific views in your application. For more information about how to configure your application’s views for element targeting, refer to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/AnchoredTooltips"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Embedded Experiences","level":2,"anchor":"Embedded-Experiences"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/AppcuesFrameView"},{"type":"text","text":" instances in your application layouts to support embedded experience content, with a non-modal presentation. For more information about how to configure your application layouts to use frame views, refer to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/FrameConfiguring"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Debugging","level":2,"anchor":"Debugging"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/URLSchemeConfiguring"},{"type":"text","text":" for setup instructions and then refer to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Debugging"},{"type":"text","text":" for usage details."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Configuring Hosting Environment","level":2,"anchor":"Configuring-Hosting-Environment"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, the Appcues SDK will send data to the United States (US) hosting environment, and no additional configuration is required. To specify a different hosting environment, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/Config\/apiHost(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/Config\/settingsHost(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"EU Hosting Environment Configuration","level":3,"an